the growing universe of exchange-traded products in 2026. TXSE is a wholly owned subsidiary of TXSE Group Inc.</div></div><aside aria-label="Citations" class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-2"><p class="type-body-3 !mb-0 text-midnight-sky-100">Citations</p><div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1 tablet:flex-row tablet:gap-x-8"><ul class="flex flex-1 flex-col !m-0 !p-0"><li class="flex gap-1.5 type-description-1 text-midnight-sky-100"><span class="shrink-0 text-accent">1</span><span><a href="https://twitter.com/GovAbbott/status/1707518975570055463" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-midnight-sky-100 no-underline transition-colors hover:text-accent">Governor Greg Abbott</a>, 2023</span></li><li class="flex gap-1.5 type-description-1 text-midnight-sky-100"><span class="shrink-0 text-accent">2</span><span>TXSE analysis of Bureau of Economic Analysis data, through Q1 2024</span></li><li class="flex gap-1.5 type-description-1 text-midnight-sky-100"><span class="shrink-0 text-accent">3</span><span>TXSE analysis of Bureau of Economic Analysis data, through Q1 2023</span></li><li class="flex gap-1.5 type-description-1 text-midnight-sky-100"><span class="shrink-0 text-accent">4</span><span>TXSE analysis, 2024</span></li></ul><ul class="flex flex-1 flex-col !m-0 !p-0"><li class="flex gap-1.5 type-description-1 text-midnight-sky-100"><span class="shrink-0 text-accent">5</span><span>Legislative Reference Library of Texas, 1968</span></li><li class="flex gap-1.5 type-description-1 text-midnight-sky-100"><span class="shrink-0 text-accent">6</span><span><a href="https://businessintexas.com/business-sectors/major-employers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-midnight-sky-100 no-underline transition-colors hover:text-accent">Texas Economic Development Corporation</a>, 2023</span></li><li class="flex gap-1.5 type-description-1 text-midnight-sky-100"><span class="shrink-0 text-accent">7</span><span><a href="https://businessintexas.com/why-texas/" target="_bl